<title>GERMANY: Pan-German final May cpi inflation +1.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pan-German final May cpi inflation +1.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>GERMAN CPI INFLATION</p>
<p>		     May 97    April 97     May 96</p>
<p>Month-on-month change (pct)</p>
<p>		    +0.4	  unch	 +0.2</p>
<p>Yr-on-yr change (pct)</p>
<p>		    +1.6	  +1.4	 +1.7</p>
<p>Index (base 1991)</p>
<p>		    118.4	 117.9	116.5</p>
<p>FINAL WEST GERMAN CPI INFLATION</p>
<p>		   May 97    April 97     May 96 Month-on-month</p>
<p>change (pct)</p>
<p>		   +0.4	  -0.2	 +0.3 Yr-on-yr change</p>
<p>(pct)</p>
<p>		   +1.5	  +1.3	 +1.5</p>
<p>Index (base 1991)</p>
<p>		   115.8	 115.3	114.1 EAST GERMAN CPI</p>
<p>INFLATION</p>
<p>		   May 97    April 97     May 96 Month-on-month</p>
<p>change (pct)</p>
<p>		   +0.4	  +0.2	 +0.1 Year-on-year</p>
<p>		   +1.8	  +1.5	 +2.8 Index (base 1991)</p>
<p>		   138.2	 137.7	135.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets.</p>
</text>
